    "text": "No one can remember the price of anything for long. As long as the rise in prices is slow enough, people get used to it. Believe it or not, around 1960 $20,000/yr was considered a very good salary. Gasoline was 30 cents a gallon, and yet you would still drive around looking for someplace where it was 29 cents. A penny was still worth a penny, and you would always have several of them in your pocket. A house cost around $80,000, and a new car around $3,000. Now it's 80 years later, and $20,00/yr makes you desperately poor.",
